
[R] the slot rows
  GREEN R1    three occupied slots: "Slot N  <leader>" over the place, indented under the name
  GREEN R2    an empty slot: EMPTY and no metadata at all ("Slot 3  EMPTY|")
  GREEN R2b   an empty slot shows no leftover name or place
  GREEN R3    an 8-letter name with both tags and the longest place each fit 36 cells: "Slot 1  Shamino1  CURRENT, RECOVERED|        Lord British's Castle"
  GREEN R4    an over-long name keeps 8 letters; a place holds 23 characters, so its row is at most 31 cells: "Slot 1  Shamino1  CURRENT|        Palace of Blackthorn an"
  GREEN R5    the tag marks the marked slot only, and no slot when none is marked
  GREEN R6    a recovered slot is tagged RECOVERED and still shows what loads: "Slot 2  Avery     RECOVERED|        Britannia"
  GREEN R7    a slot with nothing loadable is DAMAGED (neither EMPTY nor a journey), with no metadata
  GREEN R8    the confirm pages' identity: leader and place of what a load restores

[S] System Menu -> Save Game
  GREEN S1    Save Game: Slots 1-3, the live journey's slot CURRENT and selected: Slot 1  Kojac|        Lord British's Castle ; Slot 2  Avery     CURRENT|        Britannia ; Slot 3  EMPTY|
  GREEN S1b   CURRENT stays on the journey's slot when the cursor moves (it is not the selection)
  GREEN S2    an empty slot saves at once (no question)
  GREEN S3    an occupied slot asks, naming THAT slot and its own save ("Overwrite Slot 1?" / "Kojac, Lord British's Castle"), No selected
  GREEN S4    Enter on the default answer keeps the slot, back on the Save page on that slot
  GREEN S5    Back with Yes highlighted cancels: Back never confirms
  GREEN S6    the Mic (Cancel) with Yes highlighted cancels too
  GREEN S7    Yes saves into the slot the question named (Slot 1)
  GREEN S8    with no live journey's slot nothing is CURRENT and the page starts on the first empty slot
  GREEN S9    replacing a damaged slot asks too (No first), naming it a damaged save

[L] System Menu -> Load Game
  GREEN L1    Load Game: the Save page's rows and tags, on the journey's slot: Slot 1  Kojac     RECOVERED|        Lord British's Castle ; Slot 2  Avery     CURRENT|        Britannia ; Slot 3  EMPTY|
  GREEN L2    an empty slot refuses, politely, and the page stays
  GREEN L3    Down from Slot 3 wraps to Slot 1
  GREEN L4    the recovered slot's footer says what Enter does
  GREEN L5    a recovered slot loads -- that slot (its fallback is the service's)
  GREEN L6    a damaged slot is listed DAMAGED and refuses; nothing else is loaded in its place
  GREEN L7    Load's intent is always the selected slot (no cross-slot fallback is asked for)
  GREEN L8    the Mic on the Load page returns to the root (nothing loads)

[T] the title
  GREEN T1    Journey Onward names what Continue resumes: "Latest: Slot 2, Avery, Britannia" / "Enter continues Slot 2; Mic returns"
  GREEN T2    Continue is still one Enter (ContinueLatest, no question)
  GREEN T3    Continue on a recovered slot says the one before loads: "Latest save damaged; Enter loads the one before"
  GREEN T4    the title's Load Game marks Continue's slot LATEST and starts on it: Slot 1  Kojac|        Lord British's Castle ; Slot 2  Avery     LATEST, RECOVERED|        Britannia ; Slot 3  Iolo|        Iolo's Hut
  GREEN T5    Up from Slot 1 wraps to Slot 3
  GREEN T6    the Mic leaves Load Game for Journey Onward, on Load Game
  GREEN T7    a blank card: Journey Onward says so

[P] PC Save Transfer
  GREEN P1    P reaches PC Save Transfer; Import lists the slots as the other pages do, on the first empty: Slot 1  EMPTY| ; Slot 2  Avery     LATEST|        Britannia ; Slot 3  Iolo|        Iolo's Hut
  GREEN P2    importing over an occupied slot asks, naming its save; No first
  GREEN P3    the Mic cancels the import question
  GREEN P4    re-importing the same PC files asks first, No selected
  GREEN P5    Export lists the same rows, on Continue's slot
  GREEN P6    exporting an empty slot refuses

